    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22648546
    description: "Concept DOI, always resolves to the latest version"
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.22648547
    description: "Version DOI of release 0.1.0"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.1
date-released: "2026-09-07"
abstract: >-
  Public datasets of protein stability changes upon point mutation (ddG)
  disagree on the sign convention, and the disagreement is undocumented.
  FireProtDB and S2648 report opposite signs for 395 of 431 shared mutations,
  and FireProtDB is inconsistent within itself: its ProTherm-derived rows are
  flipped while its MegaScale-derived rows are not. Q3421 and Q3214, two files
  in the same repository, hold the same 3214 mutations with identical
  magnitudes and opposite signs. ddgnorm records the convention of each source
  in a curated table, together with the method and the numbers used to verify
  it, and converts nine sources into one frame with a fixed convention
  (negative is destabilizing, kcal/mol). A check command flags flipped signs,
  unit mistakes, contradictory duplicates and shifted position numbering.
keywords:
  - protein stability
  - ddG
  - data curation
  - sign convention
  - FireProtDB
  - ThermoMutDB
  - S2648
  - S669
  - Ssym
  - megascale
